	(text "ADF5904 RX + BASEBAND (Task 14)\\nU6 = ADF5904, 4-channel 24 GHz Rx downconverter.\\nRF inputs RX1-4 and LO_IN are DC-biased on-chip; AC-couple per adf5904.md p.9. 100pF coupling value is an independent engineering choice (no discrete RX-side coupling cap shown in ev-radar-mmic2.md; Fig.23 there covers AVDD decoupling, not RF/LO coupling) pending eval-BOM/vendor confirmation (BOM-lock watch item).\\nBaseband RXn_O/RXn_OB (differential, 900ohm diff Z, +-20mV DC offset) -> light series-R/shunt-C per channel -> BBn_P/BBn_N hierarchical labels. Assumption: the 100R/100pF network presents ~2.2kOhm differential load to the baseband outputs, lighter than the 900Ohm datasheet reference load; datasheet does not specify a minimum load, so this is flagged as an assumption and expected to be benign.\\nPolarity convention: RXn_O (non-inverted, datasheet-listed first) -> BBn_P; RXn_OB (complementary) -> BBn_N. Applied identically on all 4 channels.\\nAVDD (pins 4/21/27, single 3.3V rail) decoupled with 0.1uF+1nF+10pF triads per pin, from +3V3_RX (per ev-radar-mmic2.md Fig.23 RX12_AHI/RX34_AHI/LO_AHI banks).\\nAll GND pins (1,3,5,7,18,20,22,24,28,30) + EPAD(33) -> GND. ATEST(15) left unconnected (test/debug only, no-connect flag).\\nStandalone sheet: LO_OUT/RX1-4/SPI_*/LE_5904/CE_RX are hierarchical labels only; Task 15 wires this sheet's instance into the root schematic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 12.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0e67bc18-500d-44bf-9f98-cb28df903ead")
	)
